WEBVTT

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:03.623
Agents sometimes stop and wait for you:

00:00:03.623 --> 00:00:06.944
to answer a question, or to allow something.

00:00:06.944 --> 00:00:10.943
Let's give this one a task where it has to ask first.

00:00:11.351 --> 00:00:16.877
The agent is waiting. Its card in the sidebar turns amber and says so.

00:00:17.219 --> 00:00:24.995
Mission control gets a badge, and so does the project's tab, so you notice it from anywhere in FlightDeck.

00:00:24.995 --> 00:00:31.011
Desktop notifications can tell you too, even when FlightDeck is in the background.

00:00:31.405 --> 00:00:34.804
The question itself is in the agent's terminal.

00:00:34.804 --> 00:00:37.117
Pick an answer, and press Enter.

00:00:38.946 --> 00:00:41.686
And it carries on, with your answer.

00:00:42.370 --> 00:00:45.604
Done. Waiting agents never block the others:

00:00:45.604 --> 00:00:49.058
they keep working while this one waits for you.
